From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dplayx: IDirectPlaySP and IDPLobbySP: MRU lists, CreateAddress, CreateCompoundAddress, GetPlayerFlags, the lobby provider callbacks

The interfaces DirectPlay gives to service providers:

IDirectPlaySP
- AddMRUEntry / EnumMRUEntries: the most recently used lists are kept for the
  user in the registry (HKCU\<section>\<key>, value "0" is the newest),
  entries that are added again move to the front, the list is cut at the
  maximum.
- CreateAddress / CreateCompoundAddress: the compound address (Unicode
  element types are recognised).
- GetPlayerFlags: the flags the player was created with, DPERR_INVALIDPLAYER.
- QueryInterface logs a WARN for what it does not have (E_NOINTERFACE).

IDPLobbySP (what the lobby server tells DirectPlay): CreateGroup,
CreateGroupInGroup, AddGroupToGroup, AddPlayerToGroup (makes the remote
player known), DeleteGroupFromGroup, DeletePlayerFromGroup, DestroyGroup,
Set(Group|Player)Name, SetSessionDesc, HandleMessage (queued for the local
players), SendChatMessage (DPSYS_CHAT), StartSession (DPSYS_STARTSESSION with
the connection settings), EnumSessionsResponse (the session is cached like
an answer of a name server), Get/SetSPDataPointer. Without a lobby provider
session they are DPERR_UNINITIALIZED / DPERR_NOSESSIONS.
A lobby session no longer calls a missing SendToGroupEx.

